summary: 'The v1 prize is delivered: Warpline (renamed from Loom this session, TD-2026-06-23-285) now lifts real TypeScript CODE into the WARP as meaning, not just .purpose symbols — closing the TD-806 "0 deltas on a .ts-only change" gap. Built in 3 verified stages on branch warpline-ast-spike: (1) ts-essence (pure-syntactic Code Canonical Normal Form — scope-correct alpha-normalization, false-EQUAL modifier guard, type-param namespace, literal normalization); (2) ts-lens (one ts.Program over a FIXED compiler baseline, checker for identity-resolution-ONLY, free refs classified local/extern/builtin/unresolved, extern ids from syntactic import specifiers — node_modules-free; TS exact-pinned 5.9.3); (3a) essence-hash code-unit branch (body with f:idx substituted INLINE via the shared edgeEssence resolver → SCC + Merkle-by-target free; per-node version tag essence:v1:ts5.9.3:) + injectCodeUnits + absorb wired read-only; (3b) sem-delta bodyChanged/''body'' slot + predict ''body'' scalar-conflict-slot. The whole pipeline (lift→essence→diff→predict) sees code. Determinism — the thesis — holds: byte-identical stateId across two real-code absorbs (151 code-units from this package); Jinx''s checker-determinism kill-shot refuted for the pinned-compiler model. Falsifiable gates all green (frontier EQUAL = cross-symbol rename closes; call-order DIFFER = the §4.1 inline-positional payoff; code-level KNOT + DANGLE; local-rename = zero-delta). Suite 92/92. REMAINING CAPSTONE: the code-level oracle divergeMeaningOnly fixture (git-clean-but-Warpline-catches-it on CODE — the definitive demo). Branches/page still named loom (loom-presentation) — retheme later. Pending: trademark sweep on Warpline.'
