body: |-
  DESIGN CRUX (worth remembering): the spec's original "code-unit body is just another contract slot, ~6 lines" was UNSOUND — it loses call order (helper();other(); would false-EQUAL other();helper();). The fix (spec §4.1): the body carries positional f:idx tokens; stage 3 substitutes f:idx → essence(references.filter(kind==='local')[idx]) INLINE at the body slot, reusing the SAME edgeEssence resolver computeEssences already passes (so intra-SCC → @scc-internal and Merkle-by-target rename-closure come for free). This is the load-bearing subtlety; the call-order-DIFFER test is its falsifiable guard. Found by reasoning through the design before building, not after.

  PROCESS: each stage built by a TS-capable builder against a precise spec, then independently verified by re-running + reading the load-bearing code + adversarial CLI checks (the real `warpline absorb` on this repo: 151 code-units, v1 tags, byte-identical stateId twice). "A green build is not proof" held — the verification was real, not assumed.

  COMMITS this arc-session: e005f459 (merge engine→main experimental) · 75b6e20a (spike) · a3667841 (spec) · 30758261 (stage 1) · abbda54f (Loom→Warpline rename) · 0b1be782 (stage 2) · eebf1a6a (stage 3a) · df6a87e8 (stage 3b). All on warpline-ast-spike (off main); main has only the read-only Phase-1 engine (experimental). NOT pushed.
